1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,966
[beeping]

2
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:13,388
[sighs]

3
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:15,640
[groans]

4
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,226
[moans]

5
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:21,521
Yah-hoo!

6
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:24,024
-Yay! Yay! Yay! Yay!
-[Tsukasa] Hey.

7
00:00:24,107 --> 00:00:25,525
-Woo-hoo. Woo-hoo.
-[Junta] Um…

8
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:26,901
Your friend?

9
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:28,862
Great question.

10
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:31,865
The name's Junta Hayami,
we're childhood friends.

11
00:00:32,782 --> 00:00:34,951
Did-- Did you sleep here?

12
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:38,496
This is my friend, Kazuki. Funny story,
he has a string of back luck,

13
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,957
so he's gonna be crashing here
at my place for now.

14
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,960
He's… crashing here?

15
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,296
Yeah, it's a really long story.

16
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:48,298
-I'm just gonna go.
-[Riri giggling, cheering]

17
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:49,215
Yeah. Sure.

18
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,634
[groans]
I forgot my bag.

19
00:00:54,053 --> 00:00:55,013
Hmm.

20
00:00:56,765 --> 00:00:57,974
[sighs]

21
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:01,061
[Tsukasa] He's tall.

22
00:01:01,561 --> 00:01:03,146
[Junta] He's really good-looking.

23
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:10,862
[theme music]

24
00:02:34,112 --> 00:02:35,113
-[grunts, roars]
-[yells]

25
00:02:35,196 --> 00:02:37,949
#4 THE CHILDHOOD FRIEND IS EASY MODE

26
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:39,075
A victory!

27
00:02:40,201 --> 00:02:41,035
[grunts]

28
00:02:41,119 --> 00:02:43,454
[groans, yells]

29
00:02:45,665 --> 00:02:48,459
-Hey! Explain yourself, you devil!
-[Riri] Wait! I'm Riri!

30
00:02:48,543 --> 00:02:51,087
Your helpful wizard friend, not the devil!

31
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,715
You're no friend of mine.

32
00:02:53,798 --> 00:02:57,969
And what's with that guy out there?
He keeps saying we're childhood friends.

33
00:02:58,052 --> 00:03:00,471
Reuniting with a childhood friend.

34
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:02,974
Another classic romance scenario.

35
00:03:03,057 --> 00:03:04,434
ROMANTIC THRILLER

36
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:07,896
[Riri] The two of you grew up together.
You were inseparable.

37
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:12,984
Before you know it, those feelings
of friendship turned into sparks of love.

38
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:14,485
-…the problem here.
-Let me take a look at it.

39
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:19,240
What? I don't remember having a friend
like that, especially one that's so cute.

40
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:22,160
Well, his name is Junta Hayami.

41
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:24,954
And you've been besties
since elementary school.

42
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:26,748
But it's a lie. It's not true!

43
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:31,127
Junta's the hottest rookie
on the school's baseball team this year.

44
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:33,254
After being separated
for three long years,

45
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:35,006
you've been reunited.

46
00:03:35,089 --> 00:03:37,008
[Anzu] That's an oddly specific backstory.

47
00:03:37,091 --> 00:03:39,260
I haven't even told you the best part yet.

48
00:03:39,844 --> 00:03:44,015
Junta's had a secret crush on you
since elementary school!

49
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:45,516
Don't do this to him!

50
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:50,271
[Riri] Do you get it? All you have to do
to win the game is accept his feelings.

51
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:54,359
I call it Easy Mode in Romantic Thriller.

52
00:03:54,442 --> 00:03:56,277
You call this "Easy Mode"!

53
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:58,363
Just go away, devil.

54
00:03:58,863 --> 00:04:00,406
Now, begone, evil spirit!

55
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:03,284
I've already told you
I'm not the devil or an evil spirit.

56
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:06,704
How did I end up
in such a ridiculous spot?

57
00:04:06,788 --> 00:04:09,874
When you think about it,
it's not all that ridiculous.

58
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:13,628
Having a crush on your best friend
is a classic scenario.

59
00:04:13,711 --> 00:04:16,089
Hey, stop putting
these dumb thoughts into my head.

60
00:04:16,172 --> 00:04:17,799
You're cute when you're embarrassed.

61
00:04:17,882 --> 00:04:19,509
-Who you're calling cute?
-[groans]

62
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:21,511
[footsteps]

63
00:04:21,594 --> 00:04:24,597
[Anzu] Crap, what was his name? Jun… Jo…

64
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:26,015
-[Riri] You mean Junta?
-[door closes]

65
00:04:26,599 --> 00:04:30,019
Yeah, he's been out there
for a while now, hasn't he?

66
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:33,022
Oh, don't worry. I took care of that.

67
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:38,027
He's in his own scenario, see? He's been
chatting with you this whole time.

68
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:40,530
-Kirarin!
-[Junta] Uh, sorry.

69
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:44,033
I'm not all that familiar
with torture methods.

70
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:46,411
[Anzu] What the hell
were we talking about?

71
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:52,375
I got to say I was surprised earlier.

72
00:04:53,042 --> 00:04:56,045
I swear I don't usually
talk about torture.

73
00:04:56,129 --> 00:04:57,588
It wasn't about that.

74
00:04:59,173 --> 00:05:00,758
It was Kazuki.

75
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:03,219
[Anzu] Kazuki? What about him?

76
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:05,305
Look, I think it's great
that you're helping a friend

77
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:07,098
out of a bad situation,

78
00:05:07,181 --> 00:05:09,350
but it's rude of him
to put you out like that.

79
00:05:09,934 --> 00:05:13,980
Put me out? Nah, doesn't bother me.
The room was empty, anyway.

80
00:05:14,772 --> 00:05:17,734
Right, but… you sure it's a good idea?

81
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:19,861
I mean, how well do you really know him?

82
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:23,489
[Anzu] Seriously, I know a lot more
about him than I do about you.

83
00:05:24,198 --> 00:05:28,619
No worries. Kazuki's not great
at first impressions, but he's a good guy.

84
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:32,498
Besides, he's got so many fangirls,
he's totally over the whole scene.

85
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:35,668
[Junta] I see, well, okay.

86
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:38,254
I guess if your parents were cool
with him staying at your place,

87
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:40,631
then I shouldn't be
too worried about it, either.

88
00:05:41,215 --> 00:05:43,342
[Anzu] Maybe you should try
worrying less about him

89
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:45,219
and worrying more
about yourself there, buddy.

90
00:05:45,303 --> 00:05:46,637
MIND CONTROL BY THE DEVIL

91
00:05:46,721 --> 00:05:49,432
[sighs]
This whole thing is my fault.

92
00:05:49,515 --> 00:05:50,349
What?

93
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,143
Uh, nothing, really.

94
00:05:52,226 --> 00:05:54,145
[wind whooshing]

95
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:57,023
-[grunts]
-Hey, what's going on in here?

96
00:05:57,106 --> 00:05:58,900
-This wind is so strong.
-Are you okay?

97
00:05:58,983 --> 00:06:00,234
[grunts]

98
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:01,277
[Anzu] Yeah.

99
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,570
-[Junta] Anzu.
-[Anzu] Huh?

100
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:05,740
[dreamy music]

101
00:06:05,823 --> 00:06:07,158
-[heart thumping]
-H-- Hey…

102
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:09,660
Just hold still.

103
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:12,038
-[thumping continues]
-[weak moan]

104
00:06:12,121 --> 00:06:13,164
[Junta] You've got…

105
00:06:13,247 --> 00:06:15,666
a Hercules beetle stuck in your hair.

106
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:17,668
What?

107
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:19,754
[screams]
What the…

108
00:06:19,837 --> 00:06:22,256
What is that thing? It's freaking huge!

109
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,342
-[Junta] Quit squirming.
-[Anzu] Ah, no, no, no, no. Ah!

110
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:27,678
-[Junta] Oh, it's really tangled in there.
-[Anzu] Hurry up! Get it off me!

111
00:06:27,762 --> 00:06:28,805
[Junta grunts]

112
00:06:30,264 --> 00:06:31,182
Ta-da!

113
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:33,184
SINCE IT IS UNSIGHTLY,
WE'VE CONVERTED IT TO A CREPE.

114
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:35,686
Oh, gross! Get it away from me!

115
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:37,814
-Get rid of that thing!
-Uh, uh…

116
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:38,898
My bad. Sorry.

117
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:42,026
[exclaims]
Look how big this one is.

118
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:44,278
I'll bet you it's worth
at least a hundred dollars.

119
00:06:44,362 --> 00:06:48,533
One hundred?
That ugly beetle's worth that much?

120
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:50,201
[buzzing]

121
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:53,830
Stop it!

122
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:54,914
Catch it!

123
00:06:55,414 --> 00:06:57,333
-I think I can still reach it.
-[pants]

124
00:06:57,416 --> 00:06:58,334
Incoming!

125
00:06:59,001 --> 00:06:59,836
It's gonna hurt.

126
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:01,337
[yells]

127
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,339
[gasps]
Anzu!

128
00:07:08,302 --> 00:07:09,595
[buzzing]

129
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:12,682
I… got you.

130
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:14,725
[pants]

131
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:18,604
Um, nice catch. Great reflexes.

132
00:07:19,355 --> 00:07:22,066
Oh, thanks. Just glad you're okay.

133
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:26,154
[Anzu] Ugh, damn it, Junta.
Why do you have to be such a great guy?

134
00:07:26,237 --> 00:07:27,113
Uh…

135
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:28,656
What?

136
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:32,493
[Junta] It's just that beetle
really messed up your hair.

137
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:34,620
What? My hair?

138
00:07:36,664 --> 00:07:37,748
You want me to fix it?

139
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:39,417
Um…

140
00:07:40,543 --> 00:07:41,419
Could you?

141
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:46,382
[Junta] You know,
I remember in elementary school,

142
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:48,843
the kids used to call you
"Frizzy" and "Annie"

143
00:07:48,926 --> 00:07:51,012
because your hair was so red and curly.

144
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,931
[Anzu] They implanted
that memory, too. Devil!

145
00:07:54,599 --> 00:07:55,725
I remember.

146
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:57,935
Ryuya and his friends used to call me that

147
00:07:58,019 --> 00:07:59,979
because I constantly beat them at games.

148
00:08:01,731 --> 00:08:04,901
Hey, what was that one video game
you used to play all the time?

149
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:06,319
Cat Ranger?

150
00:08:06,402 --> 00:08:09,655
Yes! Cat Ranger! Oh, that was classic.

151
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:12,867
It was such an obscure game,
but it was so much fun to play.

152
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:15,870
[Junta] So, what sort of games
are you playing now?

153
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:19,749
Well, recently, they were all confiscated.

154
00:08:19,832 --> 00:08:21,375
Huh? But what happened?

155
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:23,753
[Anzu] I keep asking myself
the same thing!

156
00:08:24,837 --> 00:08:26,464
How is it going back there?

157
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:29,467
Uh, sorry, guess I'm not
so good with my hands.

158
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:30,760
[Anzu] Not good with his hands?

159
00:08:30,843 --> 00:08:32,136
-[Saki] Anzu!
-[both] Huh!

160
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:33,971
Good morning.

161
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:35,723
Hey! Morning, Saki.

162
00:08:35,806 --> 00:08:37,517
Hi, Junta. How are you?

163
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,643
Morning.

164
00:08:38,726 --> 00:08:40,603
-[Anzu] Saki knows Junta?
-[giggles]

165
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:43,481
That little devil got to her, too!

166
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:47,401
Anzu, do you want me
to help you with your hair?

167
00:08:47,485 --> 00:08:48,611
You wouldn't mind?

168
00:08:48,694 --> 00:08:50,029
That would be great.

169
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:51,322
[birds chirping]

170
00:08:52,907 --> 00:08:54,534
[Saki] There. Perfect.

171
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:56,160
You're the best.

172
00:08:56,244 --> 00:08:59,747
You know what? You should start
wearing scrunchies. You look so cute.

173
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:00,957
[laughs]

174
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,333
Junta, your thoughts?

175
00:09:02,416 --> 00:09:03,251
Me?

176
00:09:03,334 --> 00:09:04,252
[exhales]

177
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:06,003
Yeah.

178
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:10,132
[Anzu shrieks]
What's with that face?

179
00:09:11,008 --> 00:09:12,176
Oh, thanks.

180
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,137
-She totally asked him on purpose.
-[giggles]

181
00:09:17,306 --> 00:09:21,644
Well, Junta's actually a really nice guy.
I wasn't sure what to expect

182
00:09:21,727 --> 00:09:25,439
from my mysterious childhood friend
showing up out of the blue,

183
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:27,650
but it's kinda weird how comfortable it is

184
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:30,653
-just hanging out with him and Saki.
-She screams so loud.

185
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:32,822
[Anzu] It almost feels like
we really are old friends.

186
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:34,156
[laughter]

187
00:09:39,745 --> 00:09:41,205
-[Makoto] Tsukasa.
-Hm?

188
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:44,667
Morning. Happy to see
you're heading back to school today.

189
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,419
Whoa, did you get a new phone?

190
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:49,589
[Tsukasa] Yeah, can't do anything
without one, so…

191
00:09:50,298 --> 00:09:51,799
-[Rena] Tsukasa!
-Huh?

192
00:09:53,175 --> 00:09:56,596
I can't believe
you just abandoned us like that yesterday.

193
00:09:57,221 --> 00:09:59,807
And to make it worse,
you totally ditched us

194
00:09:59,890 --> 00:10:02,351
-for a girl from another class.
-[sighs]

195
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:04,979
Wait! Were you really with a girl?

196
00:10:05,062 --> 00:10:06,564
That's different.

197
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:08,232
Trust me. She's just a friend.

198
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:10,818
[gasps]
You got a new phone?

199
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:13,529
Here, let's exchange our numbers.

200
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:16,240
-I think I'll pass.
-What--

201
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:19,368
And find someone else to follow around.

202
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:23,664
No way! Meanie.

203
00:10:24,248 --> 00:10:26,626
Would it kill you to be a little nicer?

204
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:28,711
If I'm not plunged, she won't learn.

205
00:10:28,794 --> 00:10:30,504
Oh, let me get your number.

206
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:33,299
-[Makoto] You're really gonna call?
-[Tsukasa sighs]

207
00:10:33,966 --> 00:10:35,259
[groans angrily]

208
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,637
[school bell dings]

209
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:42,308
[Makoto] Whose bright idea was it
to put PE before lunch? I'm starving!

210
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:45,436
Same. Looking forward
to a home-cooked lunch.

211
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:47,813
-You always cook for yourself?
-Yeah.

212
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:50,358
[Makoto] Well,
since you're already making food,

213
00:10:50,441 --> 00:10:52,568
how about you make a little extra for me?

214
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:54,779
-[Tsukasa] No.
-[Makoto] Doesn't hurt to ask.

215
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:57,365
[Tsukasa] I'm already making two lunches.

216
00:10:57,865 --> 00:10:59,408
There's a quiz in Math.

217
00:10:59,492 --> 00:11:00,326
[gasps]

218
00:11:01,577 --> 00:11:02,411
Hello.

219
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:03,996
[Tsukasa] Hm.

220
00:11:05,498 --> 00:11:07,917
Hold up. Do you really know Junta Hayami?

221
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:08,918
Do you know him?

222
00:11:09,502 --> 00:11:12,296
Only the star rookie
of our baseball team this year.

223
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:14,674
There are rumors that he'll even go pro.

224
00:11:15,299 --> 00:11:18,803
[Tsukasa] I didn't realize Hoshino
had such a popular childhood friend.

225
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:21,389
How could you not have heard of him?

226
00:11:21,472 --> 00:11:25,059
He's out on the field practicing
almost every free period there is.

227
00:11:25,684 --> 00:11:27,603
Plus, he's tall and good-looking, too.

228
00:11:28,604 --> 00:11:30,940
Don't be jealous.
You're just as good-looking.

229
00:11:32,566 --> 00:11:34,819
-I am not jealous of that guy.
-[scoffs]

230
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:36,821
-Did you stand us up? Hey.
-Man!

231
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:38,864
He's gonna be crashing here
at my place for now.

232
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:41,283
He's… crashing here?

233
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:44,203
You said you don't wanna date
anyone right now, right?

234
00:11:44,286 --> 00:11:46,205
Oh, great! 'Cause me, too.

235
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:51,168
Yeah, we'll see.

236
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:59,135
So, hey, what do you guys know
about that guy? His name is Kazuki.

237
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:00,302
Oh, I thought you knew him.

238
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:02,471
No, I just met him this morning.

239
00:12:03,055 --> 00:12:05,057
I've heard of him.
I think he's in Class 7.

240
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:07,601
I always hear the girls
whispering about him.

241
00:12:07,685 --> 00:12:09,603
So he's pretty popular then.

242
00:12:09,687 --> 00:12:11,480
What? Does that make him your enemy?

243
00:12:12,064 --> 00:12:16,569
He's popular and smart.
He's placed top ten in the midterms.

244
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:17,486
[Junta] Top ten?

245
00:12:18,195 --> 00:12:20,072
[friend 1] That guy's
on a whole different level.

246
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,365
-[friends] Agreed.
-[sighs]

247
00:12:21,907 --> 00:12:23,993
[team manager] What's with this
slow march down the hall?

248
00:12:24,076 --> 00:12:25,161
Mind if we join?

249
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:27,663
Oh, hey, guys, look who it is.

250
00:12:27,746 --> 00:12:28,581
Hm.

251
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:32,209
Do either of you know Tsukasa Kazuki?

252
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:36,297
Kazuki? You mean
the really hot from Class 7?

253
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:38,174
Did you know he's friends with Junta?

254
00:12:38,257 --> 00:12:39,258
Jealous!

255
00:12:39,341 --> 00:12:41,010
Well, more like a friend of a friend.

256
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:45,431
Uh, question. If he asked to,
I don't know, sleepover at your place,

257
00:12:45,514 --> 00:12:46,515
would you guys let him?

258
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:49,518
-Oh, my gosh. Yes, of course, I would.
-Mm-hm.

259
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:53,022
[team manager] Then we fall in love
and live happily ever after.

260
00:12:53,606 --> 00:12:54,648
I figured.

261
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:56,734
[friend 2] What's up?
You're just as popular as him.

262
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:58,027
-Hell yeah.
-Hell yeah.

263
00:12:58,110 --> 00:13:02,448
Don't deny it, we all saw you flirting
with that cute girl you grew up with.

264
00:13:02,531 --> 00:13:03,908
You even walked her to school.

265
00:13:05,117 --> 00:13:09,622
Flirt? No, Anzu's just an old friend.
That's all it is, though…

266
00:13:09,705 --> 00:13:11,207
[friends] "Though"? Though what?

267
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:13,542
-I mean… Never mind.
-[friends grunting]

268
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:17,379
[Junta] They're right, though.
Anzu is really cute.

269
00:13:17,463 --> 00:13:19,131
Her hair, her smile…

270
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:21,926
No, I can't be thinking this stuff!

271
00:13:22,009 --> 00:13:24,762
Hey, uh, is that really helping anything?

272
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:26,680
[birds chirping]

273
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:31,894
I'm sorry, Anzu.

274
00:13:32,394 --> 00:13:34,688
I've got a broadcast club meeting
during lunch today.

275
00:13:35,356 --> 00:13:37,775
Yeah, um-hm, it's all good.

276
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:40,069
-Bye!
-[Anzu chuckles softly]

277
00:13:40,152 --> 00:13:42,655
[classmate] It's really him,
the hottest boy in Class 7.

278
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:44,782
Hoshino.

279
00:13:45,407 --> 00:13:46,242
[Anzu] Hm?

280
00:13:47,284 --> 00:13:48,244
Come here.

281
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:50,246
What?

282
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:55,084
[Saki] Wait. Are those two friends now?
I am so curious.

283
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:57,378
Ugh, but I'm gonna be late.

284
00:14:00,881 --> 00:14:03,217
[grunts]
You mixed up our lunches.

285
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:06,720
Yeah, sorry.
I'm not really a morning person.

286
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:09,974
-[Makoto] Hey, what's up?
-[Tsukasa] Hm?

287
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:11,392
Tsukasa.

288
00:14:12,059 --> 00:14:13,852
Wait, is that…

289
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:16,814
Hmm.

290
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:17,731
Lunches?

291
00:14:18,399 --> 00:14:22,611
She helped me out yesterday
when my place flooded. That's all it is.

292
00:14:23,445 --> 00:14:24,697
Whatever you say.

293
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:26,198
[Anzu] It's not untrue.

294
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:27,116
DOESN'T SUSPECT A THING

295
00:14:27,199 --> 00:14:29,493
-Keep this quiet.
-[laughs]

296
00:14:29,577 --> 00:14:32,121
I got you.
Don't want your fans overreacting.

297
00:14:33,205 --> 00:14:34,707
And you are?

298
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:36,709
I'm Anzu Hoshino.

299
00:14:36,792 --> 00:14:38,335
How's Hosshi sound?

300
00:14:38,419 --> 00:14:39,587
I'm Makoto.

301
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:43,966
So this must be the girl
Rena was talking about, huh?

302
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:45,509
What? Not me.

303
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:47,970
[Makoto] She said
Tsukasa ditched her for you.

304
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:49,555
[Anzu] Oh, right.

305
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:51,557
Well, let's go.

306
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:56,395
This is the perfect place for lunch.

307
00:14:56,478 --> 00:14:57,521
Right, Hosshi?

308
00:14:57,605 --> 00:14:59,899
Oh, okay. Makoto's great.

309
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:02,026
-He's this nice with everyone?
-Yup.

310
00:15:02,943 --> 00:15:06,113
In case it comes up,
I told them I was staying with family.

311
00:15:06,196 --> 00:15:07,031
[Anzu] Got it.

312
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:09,658
[light music]

313
00:15:09,742 --> 00:15:13,913
[Makoto] Not fair! That looks delicious.
He refused to make me lunch.

314
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:15,039
[Tsukasa] Just returning a favor.

315
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:18,208
Kazuki is a great cook.
He's way better than I am.

316
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:20,044
That bar's set pretty low.

317
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:25,215
How about you come over and teach
my mom and sisters how to cook?

318
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:27,551
Oh, you have a lot of sisters?

319
00:15:28,469 --> 00:15:31,055
Wandering the house in robes, hair a mess…

320
00:15:31,138 --> 00:15:33,515
It's completely jaded to me
when it comes to girls.

321
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:34,850
[laughs]

322
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:37,728
Got to say I'm a little jealous.
I'm an only child.

323
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:40,105
You've got a sister. You know what I mean.

324
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:42,733
Oh, I didn't know that.
You've never even mentioned her.

325
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:45,069
[Makoto] Hey, let's see a picture of her.

326
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:47,071
I don't have one.

327
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:52,660
Hm. Makoto, is that all
you're eating for lunch?

328
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:53,744
Heck, yeah.

329
00:15:53,827 --> 00:15:55,245
[gasps]

330
00:15:55,329 --> 00:15:56,664
Chocolate!

331
00:15:56,747 --> 00:15:57,581
CHOCOLATE CORNET

332
00:15:58,165 --> 00:16:00,084
[Makoto] You want some?
I'll split it with you.

333
00:16:00,167 --> 00:16:02,586
-Really?
-Way to be cool.

334
00:16:03,212 --> 00:16:04,755
[Makoto] Here, take as much as you want.

335
00:16:04,838 --> 00:16:06,715
-[Anzu] Uh, thanks…
-[Riri] Denied!

336
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:09,468
[screams, cries]

337
00:16:09,551 --> 00:16:10,594
You okay?

338
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:13,973
Fine. Just remembered, I'm on a diet.

339
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:16,183
[Anzu] I can't believe I just said that.

340
00:16:16,266 --> 00:16:17,267
A diet? Since when?

341
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:19,728
I get it. Nothing to be ashamed of.

342
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:24,316
Hm?

343
00:16:25,025 --> 00:16:26,735
Rena, check it out.

344
00:16:26,819 --> 00:16:28,404
-No joke…
-[Makoto] Yeah.

345
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:29,822
…you should have seen his face.

346
00:16:29,905 --> 00:16:31,281
-Hilarious!
-[Makoto laughs]

347
00:16:32,324 --> 00:16:34,243
[school bell dings]

348
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:36,245
[indistinct chatter]

349
00:16:36,829 --> 00:16:38,497
[Anzu] Time to head home.

350
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:42,835
And be bored out of my mind
without any of my games to play.

351
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:45,587
Guess I could start
looking for a part-time job.

352
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:47,256
-[Rena] Hoshino.
-Hm?

353
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:48,966
Got a minute?

354
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:51,927
Sure?

355
00:16:54,388 --> 00:16:57,558
I'm looking forward to
an afternoon without practice.

356
00:16:57,641 --> 00:16:58,976
Wanna hit the arcade?

357
00:16:59,059 --> 00:17:02,813
Wait, you probably wanna catch up
with your girlfriend, don't ya?

358
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:05,858
-I told you she's just a friend.
-Yeah, whatever.

359
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:09,570
Call it what you want, but we know
you want to hang out with her. Go on!

360
00:17:11,196 --> 00:17:12,239
Thanks.

361
00:17:14,324 --> 00:17:15,159
Hey!

362
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:17,745
[both chuckle]

363
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:19,955
-You're right.
-Hm, oh…

364
00:17:20,914 --> 00:17:21,749
Junta?

365
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:25,252
If you're looking for Anzu,
I think she went home already.

366
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:27,796
Oh, really? She must have missed my text.

367
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:29,965
You can try calling her.

368
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:32,551
I've got to run out
to a meeting now. Sorry.

369
00:17:32,634 --> 00:17:34,261
Cool. Have fun.

370
00:17:34,845 --> 00:17:37,097
-Anzu is such a lucky girl.
-Um-hm.

371
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:39,266
Surrounded by hotties.

372
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:42,770
[both gasp]

373
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:44,521
-Hm.
-Hm.

374
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:50,194
Hey, hang on. Have you seen Anzu?

375
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:53,197
I can't seem to get a hold of her.

376
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,364
No, I haven't.

377
00:17:55,365 --> 00:17:57,534
Okay, sorry to bother you.

378
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:00,829
-[Tsukasa gasps]
-[Junta] Huh?

379
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:06,335
Hm, I found her. This way.

380
00:18:10,672 --> 00:18:13,092
So, uh, you wanted to talk?

381
00:18:13,675 --> 00:18:15,594
I don't think we should be here.

382
00:18:15,677 --> 00:18:18,597
-It looks like a private conversation.
-Hm.

383
00:18:19,431 --> 00:18:20,724
Tell me something.

384
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:23,227
Do you have a thing for Tsukasa?

385
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:26,230
What?
[gasping]

386
00:18:26,313 --> 00:18:28,857
Not at all. We're just good friends.

387
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:30,400
Oh, really?

388
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:33,445
You say that but you totes have a crush.

389
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:35,739
No, that's not true.

390
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:37,533
Do you expect us to believe

391
00:18:37,616 --> 00:18:40,661
you could be just friends with him
when he's that hot?

392
00:18:41,328 --> 00:18:44,206
Of course I do. Believe me.

393
00:18:45,332 --> 00:18:49,753
I am not interested.
I have no interest in dating Tsukasa.

394
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:51,296
Or anyone else, either.

395
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:54,091
So you've got nothing to worry about.

396
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:57,094
My desires are set on
much more important places.

397
00:18:57,177 --> 00:18:58,011
LIFE

398
00:18:59,096 --> 00:19:03,517
What if I was going after him?
It's a free country, you know.

399
00:19:04,101 --> 00:19:05,519
-You're right.
-Mm-hm.

400
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:06,895
[Anzu] That was easy.

401
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:08,856
[Rena] So…

402
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:12,901
Will you help me get his attention
since he's your friend?

403
00:19:13,485 --> 00:19:14,903
You need help?

404
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:16,238
Duh!

405
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:19,950
No matter how many times
I ask him out, Tsukasa always says no.

406
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:24,121
We thought you could set them up.
What do you say?

407
00:19:24,204 --> 00:19:25,831
-[Anzu] Uh…
-You're the best.

408
00:19:27,249 --> 00:19:29,418
-Here. Take my number, okay?
-[phone tapping]

409
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,253
[Rena] Talk soon.

410
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:32,754
[sighs]

411
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:36,216
[Rena] Be sure to ask him his type, okay?

412
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,176
[gasps]

413
00:19:38,343 --> 00:19:40,971
I'm so over it, seriously.

414
00:19:41,054 --> 00:19:42,806
I'm not interested in dating.

415
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:44,808
[exhales deeply]

416
00:19:45,517 --> 00:19:47,311
Sorry, can't.

417
00:19:47,394 --> 00:19:48,312
[both gasp]

418
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:49,897
Huh?

419
00:19:51,899 --> 00:19:52,983
[Rena] Excuse me?

420
00:19:53,066 --> 00:19:56,570
Kazuki told me
he's not looking to date right now.

421
00:19:58,071 --> 00:20:01,408
Out of respect for my friend,
I can't help.

422
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:04,369
[exhales]

423
00:20:04,953 --> 00:20:06,872
[Junta] She's so cool.

424
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,374
What? Seriously?

425
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:11,376
[Anzu] Crap. Is she mad?

426
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:14,880
-[girl] Anzu!
-[sighs, gasps]

427
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:17,049
Hey, there you are!

428
00:20:17,132 --> 00:20:19,426
I've been looking everywhere for you.

429
00:20:20,469 --> 00:20:21,386
Huh?

430
00:20:21,470 --> 00:20:24,389
[Anzu] Who's she?
Oh, come on. Not another one.

431
00:20:24,473 --> 00:20:26,308
-Are you ready to go home?
-Uh…

432
00:20:26,391 --> 00:20:28,310
Oh, yeah, were you able to find Junta?

433
00:20:28,393 --> 00:20:30,145
He's been looking all over for you.

434
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:31,897
[growls]

435
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:35,817
[Anzu] What's going on? Is she supposed
to be another long-lost friend?

436
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:40,405
Anzu, you never told me
you were hanging out with these two girls.

437
00:20:40,989 --> 00:20:43,325
They're only the cutest girls in Class 7!

438
00:20:43,408 --> 00:20:44,409
[both] Huh?

439
00:20:44,493 --> 00:20:47,079
-Cute! Long lashes!
-Oh…

440
00:20:47,162 --> 00:20:51,500
That pixie nose, and your hair…
You are just so pretty!

441
00:20:51,583 --> 00:20:52,918
T-- Thank you!

442
00:20:53,001 --> 00:20:55,754
Wow, such a great figure!

443
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,923
You've gotta tell me

444
00:20:58,006 --> 00:21:00,968
the secret for making
your boobs look so thick.

445
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:03,804
-Wha--
-It's not easy to make little boobs

446
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:06,723
push up so high and natural like that.
How do you do it?

447
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:07,933
-I'm super impressed!
-Hey…

448
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:11,687
[girl] You can tell me. I get it.
I'm self-conscious about mine, too.

449
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:14,106
But with yours, you worked magic,

450
00:21:14,189 --> 00:21:17,192
they look like a full C cup,
not like Anzu's at all.

451
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:20,195
[Anzu] What? Is she saying
I can make mine look like that, too?

452
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:23,240
[girl] I'm so jealous
of your push-up C cup size!

453
00:21:23,323 --> 00:21:24,199
-So huge!
-C cup?

454
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:25,867
Lovin'!

455
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:27,494
So perky!

456
00:21:27,577 --> 00:21:29,705
That's enough already, give it a rest!

457
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:33,417
But I don't think Kazuki
is the kind of guy who'd fall for that,

458
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:35,711
so you really don't have to work so hard.

459
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:37,212
[groans]

460
00:21:37,796 --> 00:21:40,924
You are rude!
And you're wrong about everything.

461
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:42,467
Let's go, Yukka.

462
00:21:42,551 --> 00:21:43,719
Coming.

463
00:21:43,802 --> 00:21:46,596
[Yukika] Yeah,
I knew they couldn't be real.

464
00:21:48,015 --> 00:21:50,100
Another job well done! Mm-hm!

465
00:21:50,183 --> 00:21:53,103
[gasps]
Wait a second.

466
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:56,106
Your cutesy little baby voice.

467
00:21:56,690 --> 00:21:59,651
Your ultra annoying blunt way of speaking.

468
00:22:00,193 --> 00:22:03,071
That oddly familiar star
hanging on your bag.

469
00:22:03,155 --> 00:22:05,782
-[Riri] Kirarin!
-[Anzu] It's you!

470
00:22:07,367 --> 00:22:09,953
-The devil!
-You're wrong.

471
00:22:10,037 --> 00:22:11,621
No devil. Riri.

472
00:22:11,705 --> 00:22:14,249
[Anzu] You're a girl now!

473
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:17,085
-[giggles]
-[Anzu groans]

474
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:20,255
A fanfare, please!

475
00:22:20,339 --> 00:22:22,382
And a big congratulations!

476
00:22:22,466 --> 00:22:24,509
Did you fall for my little trick?

477
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:27,971
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

478
00:22:28,055 --> 00:22:31,558
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

479
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:34,311
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

480
00:22:34,394 --> 00:22:36,688
[sighs]
Don't just let things be! Come on!

481
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:39,357
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

482
00:22:39,441 --> 00:22:41,359
So I can make sure I get paid.

483
00:22:41,443 --> 00:22:43,612
[closing theme music]

484
00:22:43,695 --> 00:22:44,529
♪ Ah, yeah! ♪

485
00:22:47,157 --> 00:22:47,991
♪ Let's go! ♪

486
00:22:50,535 --> 00:22:51,661
♪ Lo-love! ♪

487
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:54,581
♪ Here we go! ♪
